        "path": "wiki/macro/regime.md",
        "mode": "tldr",
        "content": "**Prior risk-on baseline overturned by Iran escalation.** The May 1 regime summary cited Iran peace talks and WTI \u22122% as the dominant catalyst shift to risk-on. That narrative reversed on May 4: reports of missile strikes on a US warship near Jask island have driven oil prices higher and Dow futures lower, returning the macro backdrop to mixed-to-cautious. The S&P 500 hit a record intraday high (7,230) on May 1 on Apple earnings; that session was the local peak before the geopolitical re-escalation. [source: web_research/NVDA.json macro_context, run 20260504_125732]",
